      "writtenOn": "2025-03-25T09:00:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think Paul has a point here. While both approaches are valid, the current code is already using manual mocking of this so the migration is expensive. I also don\u0027t think the migration buys us much, because I don\u0027t think that @FeatureFlag is necessarily easier to read than the manual mocking (it\u0027s terser, but it depends on knowing the internals of a tool and frankly the whole design where you have to pass a lambda to the rule and still manage flags manually I find more obfuscated than useful).",
